Z||000000||Lunapark||10-01-2000||08:27 PM||||I am getting a code 45. It started out as a code 34, but it has migrated to 45. I have been on this all weekend. It started when I replaced the overboard throttle body and plenum. I have now replaced the IAC, O2, MAP twice, Plugs Twice, Wires, Coil, Ignition Module, THis was all done through a process of elimination after replacing the map the first time did not fix the problem, The reason I went for the map was that the service manual says disconnect the map if the car runs good then it is the map. It won't run ( I mean you can drive it) but the black smoke goes away if the map is unplugged. The car is running rich and I don't know why. It has not always been doing this. It is a 3.4 pushrod, Crate motor, 3.4 injectors with no fuel regulator. Again car has been running fine until I swapped out the throttle body and plenum. <P>Please Help||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-01-2000||10:51 PM||||I'm no expert, sounds like something is amiss with the throttle body you swapped.  If you have the old one around, put it back on and see what happens.<BR>Isn't the thottle body what dumps gas into the plenum?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||10-02-2000||12:12 AM||||The throttle body on the V-6 only meters air into the upper intake plenum.  The 6 fuel injectors spray fuel directly into the air stream in the intake manifold just before it is sucked into the intake valve.<P>I agree with Old Lar, if you have the old throttle body put it back on and see if it works with it.||||reg||1
